---
import ReadingPage from '../layouts/ReadingPage.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<ReadingPage
  title="About ScoreSheetSquare – Free Score Sheets for Game Night"
  description="ScoreSheetSquare gives every popular game one page with free printable score sheets and an online scorekeeper. Independent and free, with no sign-up."
  heading="About ScoreSheetSquare"
  lead="One page for every game, with a score sheet to print and a score sheet to fill in on screen."
  crumb="About"
>
  <div class="measure prose">
    <h2 class="t-lead">What the site is for</h2>
    <p>
      Most people looking for a score sheet want one thing: a sheet that fits their game, ready to print. Each game here
      has a single page with that sheet in three sizes, standard, large print and two to a page, for US Letter or A4. You
      can add your players’ names before printing, or skip the paper and keep score on the sheet on screen.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is nothing to sign up for. Downloads start straight away, and games scored online stay in your own browser.
    </p>

    <h2 class="t-lead">Who runs it</h2>
    <p>
      ScoreSheetSquare is run by {site.owner}, based in {site.location}. Suggestions for games to add, and corrections to
      any sheet or scoring table, are always welcome on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="t-lead">Independent</h2>
    <p>
      ScoreSheetSquare is not affiliated with, endorsed by or connected to any game publisher. Game names are trademarks of
      their owners and are used only to say which game a sheet is for. The sheets use our own design, with no logos, box art
      or artwork from the games.
    </p>

    <h2 class="t-lead">How it is paid for</h2>
    <p>
      The site shows advertising, which keeps every sheet free. Ads are kept away from the scorekeeper and the download
      buttons so nobody taps one by mistake.
    </p>
  </div>
</ReadingPage>

<style>
  .prose { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .prose h2 { margin-block-start: 32px; }
  .prose h2:first-child { margin-block-start: 0; }
</style>
